TITLE='Authentic title "What Changes at $1M, $2M, and $5M Retirement?" is a tiered-threshold question frame. The script delivers a dense, mostly accurate tour of how Social Security share, taxes, RMDs, IRMAA, estate rules and fees change by portfolio size, plus behavioural evidence that wealthier retirees under-spend. TYPICAL at the 0.5 boundary (0.50009x) against a very young cohort; association only, no CTR evidence.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field. Left: the recurring cartoon man with a sly smile pointing right. Top right: a black headline "CHANGES EVERYTHING!". Below: three tiers labelled "$1M" (house), "$2M" (SUV) and "$5M" (yacht). The image implies bigger lifestyles at each tier, while the script argues the main changes are tax, legal and behavioural, not lifestyle. At 320x180 the headline and tier labels are legible; icons small but clear.'
SCRIPT='A tiered retirement explainer using three composite retirees (Wendy $1M, Theo $2M, Naomi $5M): restaurant hook, system framing, reality check (Fidelity and Fed medians vs means), $1M (Social Security as an annuity, 0% gains, senior deduction, sequence risk, Bengen vs Morningstar), $2M (RMDs, Social Security taxation, IRMAA, long-term care), the under-spending finding (EBRI, J.P. Morgan, Blanchett), $5M (Social Security share, RMDs, NIIT, Roth conversion inversion, state estate taxes, fees), the cost of the jump in years, happiness research, inflation and a close. Verified: EBRI spend-down, Fidelity year-end 2025 averages. Reproduces: RMDs, Social Security shares, $5.4M threshold, fee and flat-fee ratios, 8/12-year jumps, nursing-home share, inflation. Minor issues: Fidelity figures one quarter stale; "1% eats 30%" (24.5% at 7%); several statistics unfetched. The stored ending is complete.'
BEATS=['Hook: two couples, $1.1M vs $4.9M, reading the check.','Characters and system framing.','Reality check: medians vs means.','$1M: Social Security as an asset; 0% gains; senior deduction.','Sequence risk; Bengen vs Morningstar.','$2M: RMDs, Social Security taxation, IRMAA.','Long-term care.','Under-spending: EBRI, J.P. Morgan, Blanchett.','$5M: Social Security share, RMDs, NIIT, Roth conversions.','State estate taxes.','Fee drag and flat fees.','Cost of the jump in years; happiness; inflation.','Close: what would you do on Wednesday.']
